# HC HELD ON like hc-hold, but with the Balancer told to keep 2 of the 3 victim
# threads idle (HC_TARGET_IDLE_CORES=2, the maximum for a 3-thread Primary): the
# least lend-back HC allows, i.e. closest to plain sibling isolation. Shows the
# floor of the handler inflation versus the harvesting trade-off (2026-11-01).
# HarvestContainers with BANG-BANG control (motivation experiment, 2026-10-23).
# Apply on the FIRST tick with e_iso > HC_THETA_ON (HC_UP_WINDOWS=1) and a
# single threshold (HC_THETA_OFF == HC_THETA_ON; formula.go accepts equality).
# Release still waits HC_DOWN_WINDOWS ticks (100 ms each) under the
# threshold: HC removes the very contention that triggered it, so a
# zero-delay release would limit-cycle at the tick rate (each Apply/Restore
# re-registers with the Listener and restarts the Balancer). 50 = 5 s.
# Needs hc-listener running (qidlecpu loaded) on the node.
ISO_ACTUATOR=hc
N_MAX=0
HC_VICTIM_CPULIST=18,19,20
HC_SECONDARY_CPULIST=0,1,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12,13,16,17,21,22,23,24,25,26,27,28,29
HC_TARGET_IDLE_CORES=2
HC_LOW_TIC=1
HC_ACBF=0.33
HC_MIN_SECONDARY_CORES=0
HC_BALANCER_CPU=14
HC_THETA_ON=-1
HC_THETA_OFF=-2
HC_UP_WINDOWS=1
HC_DOWN_WINDOWS=1000000
